      "text": "/skill:tidy-recipe-authoring\n\nCreate tidy recipes for workbook `f6c60fc2329acd79d2f3eaf0172d67896e23ec8f4ec3a90aeb1dfc0bb4207351--recorded-crime-offenders-2014-15-cube-3-source.xlsx`.\n\n- Publication: Recorded Crime — Offenders (Australian Bureau of Statistics)\n- Release or year: 2014-15\n- Sheets needing a recipe: 5 of 5\n\n| sheet | sheet_sha256 | current recipe |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Contents\" | d28f087280774899720b85dda5ac0ddf606a850709a595f23d60347377436dd8 | missing |\n| \"Table_18\" | 4b1f8d05c532f8d7628b6d6822cfd99a34aba493d1070838e006f34d0d07bcde | missing |\n| \"Table_19\" | afe200ba59785544ba1cd44a114eb051b886882f4d6516b8f146c3e92c5ee68b | missing |\n| \"Table_20\" | c34f532907b2cf6ef18dc2d375449313d2127234dbfe88c7a0bfcac12533f300 | missing |\n| \"Table_21\" | 81064d82697e17290251906766dc20d8f6edb18cf2116724ab65dd25400c85b9 | missing |\n\nRelated workbooks:\n- None\n\nWork through every sheet listed above using the skill's workflow. Use\n`codemode` scripts to call the recipe tools, and batch the work: for example,\nlist the workbook and check templates for all sheets in one script, then read\ngrids and test recipes a few sheets at a time. Keep script output short.\n\nName dimensions from `dictionary/dimensions.csv` (see the skill's\n`references/naming.md`); declare any name it lacks in `new_dimensions`.\n\nWrite each recipe to `tidy-recipes/<sheet_sha256>.json` and finish every sheet\nwith `submit_recipe`. You may only write recipe files for this workbook.\n\nEnd with one line per sheet: `sheet | kind | status | records | remaining failures`."
